<h4>Security</h4>
<p>Paygenius uses appropriate administrative, technical, and physical security measures to protect Data about Paygenius Customers.</p>

<ol>
    <li><p>Card Holder's Data Security Policy</p></li>
    <li><p>The security of card information shared by the Customers is of paramount importance for Paygenius. Stringent security measures are implemented while designing the Paygenius's payment processing mechanism, to safeguard the privacy of the information shared by the Customers. In order to achieve complete protection to card details of the Customers, Paygenius maintains the compliance with the guidelines issued by PCI, NPCI-Rupay, RBI, Visa “Account Information Security Programme” and the MasterCard “Site Data Protection Programme” and any other similar program as stipulated by the Card Schemes and any changes to those programmes and standards which may occur from time to time.</p></li>
    <li><p>The Customer Card credentials such as debit card/ credit card number, bank account number etc. are not accessible to Paygenius as Paygenius uses the card tokenization services for processing the transactions in compliance to RBI circulars CO.DPSS.POLC.No.S-516/02-14-003/2021-22 dated September 07, 2021 pertaining to Tokenisation – Card Transactions: Permitting Card-on-File Tokenisation (CoFT) Services and CO.DPSS.POLC.No.S-760/02-14-003/2022-23 dated July 28, 2022 pertaining to Restriction on Storage of Actual Card Data [i.e. Card-on-File (CoF)]; therefore, the Paygenius neither stores nor share the card details to any third party.</p></li>
    <li><p>Additionally, the Paygenius maintains relevant policies to protect the personal information from unauthorized access, use and disclosure which are reviewed from time to time, in order to improve the security of information shared by the Customers and regular audits are conducted by Paygenius to ensure compliance with Payments Card Information Security Standard Council (PCI) in respect of protecting card data.</p></li>
</ol>


